- description: Code quality queries ABOM runs against its own C#

# Pinned for the reason abom-go-quality.qls states: an unpinned reference downloads whatever is
# newest, so the finding count moves without the code moving.
- import: codeql-suites/csharp-security-and-quality.qls
  from: codeql/csharp-queries
  version: 1.10.0

# Read and rejected, 2026-09-10 — the only rule this suite excludes, and it stays the exception.
#
# All four hits are Blazor boundaries: two timer callbacks and two button handlers. Nothing
# encloses them, so an exception allowed to escape is not reported anywhere — it tears down the
# circuit or silently stops the poll, leaving the page frozen on stale data with no sign of why.
# Each of the four already records the message into a field the reader can see, which is the
# behavior this rule exists to get. Narrowing them would mean enumerating the exception types
# `ReadFromJsonAsync` can raise and being wrong about one.
#
# It is excluded rather than removed from the pack so a fifth occurrence in a *service* — where an
# outer handler does exist — still has to be argued for here rather than passing unnoticed.
- exclude:
    id: cs/catch-of-all-exceptions
